WEBVTT

00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:05.400
The AV-98,
aka the Ingram patrol labor.

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:08.520
6.02 tons.
8.02 meters high.

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:12.700
SCB powered.
SCLM drive system.

00:00:12.990 --> 00:00:15.990
Armed and ready for combat with a
37 millimeter revolver and stun baton.

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:19.540
Designed specifically
for police use...

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:22.200
to make a psychological impact
on the community...

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:25.540
to deter criminals
while making the public feel safe.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:51.280
yume wo sutenaide
You must not let go of your dreams

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:54.070
me wo sorasanaide
And never turn your gaze away

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:59.080
futari no ai mo kumoru yo
Yet even still love may cloud up and fade away

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:03.450
utsumuita kata wo
And even though you comforted your love

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:06.290
dakishimeta keredo
When he was feeling down

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:11.300
samishisa mune ni tsumotta
Sadness was still weighing down his heavy heart

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:18.510
yume wa kimi no buki no hazu da yo
Hang on tight to your dreams - they're weapons in your arsenal

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:25.270
nee da kara kanashimi mo kinukete itte
You'll find that you can get through anything at all

00:01:25.770 --> 00:01:31.440
so never cry itsu mo kimi wo mitsumete 'ru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be watching over you

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:37.280
fair na ikikata no kimi ga suki
What I love about you is your strong sense of fairness

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:43.790
so never cry itsu mo kimi no soba ni iru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be right there by your side

00:01:44.410 --> 00:01:49.460
da kara mata asu e kakedashite
And so now you can face your future fearlessly

00:02:01.850 --> 00:02:05.100
So you want us to visit
your labs in Tsuchiura...

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:08.980
capture Utsumi, and take
command of the Griffin.

00:02:09.270 --> 00:02:12.980
He thinks it's his personal toy.
Who knows what he'll do?

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:15.440
You're authorized to
use any means necessary.

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:20.030
Leave it to Shaft Security Systems.

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:25.240
The Dogs of Shaft

00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:43.760
Crazy driver!

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:45.970
It's Shaft Security Systems.

00:02:45.970 --> 00:02:46.680
You know them?

00:02:46.970 --> 00:02:51.850
Three-S. I guess you haven't
heard of them in Japan, yet.

00:02:52.520 --> 00:02:54.770
They have quite a rep in Southeast Asia.

00:02:55.190 --> 00:02:56.900
They're almost a private army.

00:02:57.440 --> 00:02:58.360
An army?

00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:01.200
Yes. Owned and operated by Shaft.

00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:08.450
The Division Manager
is losing faith in me.

00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:10.750
He never <i>had</i> any faith in you.

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:12.670
What a cruel thing to say!

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:15.000
Just a fact.

00:03:20.470 --> 00:03:24.640
I'm sorry, Chief Utsumi,
but you can't leave the building.

00:03:24.850 --> 00:03:29.600
How distressing!
They already barred me from Tokyo.

00:03:30.020 --> 00:03:32.810
I'm very sorry, but I have my orders.

00:03:35.810 --> 00:03:37.900
Back to the office, Kurosaki.

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:40.240
Yeah, we could hardly fight them.

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:41.400
Hardly.

00:03:44.110 --> 00:03:44.740
Not a chance.

00:03:51.250 --> 00:03:52.330
Stop!

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:54.380
Don't move.

00:03:56.290 --> 00:03:58.090
I guarantee, this will hurt.

00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:02.760
It's loaded and ready.
What next, Chief?

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:06.180
They can't run the Griffin without me.

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:08.720
How did we get
dragged into this mess?

00:04:09.220 --> 00:04:12.980
I regret our choice of associates...

00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:15.560
but we have to see this
thing through to the end.

00:04:20.690 --> 00:04:24.530
Bring the car around!
Hurry, or Three-S will have us!

00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:30.200
What? You let Utsumi get away?

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:40.880
Head for Tokyo.

00:04:51.640 --> 00:04:52.430
Detective Matsui!

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:54.060
So, he's finally come out.

00:04:57.440 --> 00:05:01.730
Hello? Second Section.
Chiba Prefectural Police? Go on.

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:10.990
Who's fixing the chow tonight?

00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:13.750
That would be Izumi!

00:05:13.750 --> 00:05:15.000
Bad news.

00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:20.170
That's mean, Captain!
I poured my heart into this meal!

00:05:20.500 --> 00:05:22.670
Sorry, I wasn't talking about dinner.

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:29.800
I have to tell you before we eat.
I've just heard from Chiba.

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:34.600
I'm afraid the Black Labor we
fought in Haruumi <i>didn't</i> crash.

00:05:35.930 --> 00:05:37.600
What do you mean?

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:38.810
How do they know?

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:43.780
The fragments were deliberately
scattered around the crash site.

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:45.780
That would need advance preparation.

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:51.490
They found two right arms
and some outdated hydraulics.

00:05:51.490 --> 00:05:53.790
So the crash was deliberately faked.

00:05:53.790 --> 00:05:58.870
And then they removed the real
Labor right under our noses!

00:05:58.870 --> 00:06:01.540
Why go to all the trouble?

00:06:01.540 --> 00:06:07.630
It bought them time. We weren't
searching for the Black Labor.

00:06:08.220 --> 00:06:09.590
Will we see it again?

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:11.300
I hope not.

00:06:11.470 --> 00:06:12.890
I'd bet on it.

00:06:12.890 --> 00:06:14.890
The question is when?

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:20.230
Hey!

00:06:20.690 --> 00:06:21.440
What?

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:22.400
You know.

00:06:22.820 --> 00:06:26.440
If he comes back,
we'll have to fight him.

00:06:26.990 --> 00:06:29.110
I need to start building
up my strength.

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:34.950
Three trailers are fleeing
the research center.

00:06:34.950 --> 00:06:39.080
They appear to be heading
for Port Kashima. I repeat...

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:43.250
Our pursuit cars would
be too conspicuous.

00:06:43.420 --> 00:06:44.670
Perhaps it's time for subtlety.

00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:49.680
Get me the Tokyo maps.

00:06:54.220 --> 00:06:58.100
Looks bad! Who knows
what Utsumi will try now?

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:01.810
The <i>Sangria</i> is docked
tonight in Port Kashima.

00:07:02.270 --> 00:07:05.190
You don't think he's planning
to load the Griffin, do you?

00:07:08.440 --> 00:07:10.280
Yes? Utsumi!

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:15.120
Greetings, oh brilliant
Division Manager!

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:18.120
Doesn't the <i>Sangria</i> belong
to our Far East Manager?

00:07:18.120 --> 00:07:20.210
I'm sure he'd love to help out.

00:07:20.210 --> 00:07:24.960
But don't worry! I promise
to bring the Griffin back to Tokyo.

00:07:24.960 --> 00:07:28.300
I'd love to chat, but I've got to run.

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:31.380
I'll arrive in Tokyo around midnight.

00:07:31.380 --> 00:07:34.970
Then you'll see what
the Griffin can REALLY do.

00:07:35.510 --> 00:07:37.260
What the Griffin can really do?

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:42.060
I thought I'd let that sink in.

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:45.150
Someone lit a fire under my tail.

00:07:47.570 --> 00:07:49.150
This is all your fault.

00:07:53.410 --> 00:07:55.530
I finally stood up to him!

00:07:56.490 --> 00:08:00.250
I hate to interrupt your moment
of triumph, but we have a bug.

00:08:03.210 --> 00:08:07.170
Let them go, Kurosaki.
That bug will bring us sweet pollen.

00:08:07.790 --> 00:08:10.710
What do you think is in those trailers?

00:08:10.710 --> 00:08:13.130
I've been wondering about that.

00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:16.090
You don't suppose...

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:35.570
I expected that.

00:08:37.780 --> 00:08:39.990
I thought you were sound asleep.

00:08:41.410 --> 00:08:43.330
You must be Lt. Kanuka Clancy.

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:44.250
Yes.

00:08:45.710 --> 00:08:48.750
I never expected us to meet like this.

00:08:48.750 --> 00:08:50.050
How are you feeling?

00:08:50.050 --> 00:08:51.960
I'm afraid that was a bit of a strain.

00:08:52.630 --> 00:08:53.260
Sorry.

00:08:54.130 --> 00:08:59.970
Lt. Kumagami, I'll be brief.
Richard Wong is cornered.

00:09:00.260 --> 00:09:04.480
If he has the Black Labor,
do you think he'll use it?

00:09:04.980 --> 00:09:06.270
He's cornered?

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:08.560
Three-S is closing in on him, too.

00:09:09.440 --> 00:09:10.360
I see.

00:09:12.530 --> 00:09:17.160
Yes, he'll definitely use it.
He's that kind of man.

00:09:18.070 --> 00:09:18.820
Thank you.

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:22.660
I'll avenge you.

00:09:23.080 --> 00:09:24.370
There's no need for that.

00:09:25.410 --> 00:09:28.540
I have never considered
Richard Wong my enemy.

00:09:31.630 --> 00:09:32.460
Take care.

00:09:41.260 --> 00:09:43.470
We have a total of four M5 units.

00:09:43.850 --> 00:09:48.190
M5's? Are the Abrahams
a match for the Griffin?

00:09:48.900 --> 00:09:54.280
We'll move two onto the <i>Sangria</i>
before he can off-load the Griffin.

00:09:54.650 --> 00:09:56.700
We can trap him at the Castle Gate.

00:09:58.160 --> 00:09:59.620
The Babylon "Castle Gate?"

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:04.910
It's between two artificial islands,
Kisarazu and Kawasaki.

00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:08.170
It's like the gates in
the Panama Canal...

00:10:08.170 --> 00:10:10.580
and it's the Babylon Project's
strategic point.

00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:12.340
I know that.

00:10:12.340 --> 00:10:17.550
It's a pier they're building in
anticipation of a rising sea level.

00:10:18.180 --> 00:10:20.720
They've brought in a lot more Labors...

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:25.140
which has led to an overall
increase in Labor crime.

00:10:29.020 --> 00:10:32.690
I'm saying that if Richard Wong
gets a boat in Kashima...

00:10:32.690 --> 00:10:35.980
then heads for Tokyo,
as Detective Matsui predicts...

00:10:35.980 --> 00:10:40.160
Three-S will try to intercept
him at the Castle Gate.

00:10:41.030 --> 00:10:41.780
Your reasoning?

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:44.530
One: A surprise attack
is possible there.

00:10:44.530 --> 00:10:49.000
Two: Three-S wants to avoid
confronting the Japanese police.

00:10:49.710 --> 00:10:53.130
You predict violence in the open waters,
outside our jurisdiction.

00:10:53.130 --> 00:10:53.630
Yes.

00:10:55.500 --> 00:10:57.880
I'll have to consider this.

00:11:28.500 --> 00:11:32.500
Yes. I'm well aware that this
is based purely on intuition.

00:11:33.130 --> 00:11:35.710
I'll handle the paperwork later.

00:11:36.460 --> 00:11:38.300
Thank you.

00:11:40.220 --> 00:11:41.090
Well, then.

00:11:47.060 --> 00:11:49.060
Thank you all for working so late.

00:11:49.270 --> 00:11:52.020
I want to help however I can,
so I made everyone tea.

00:11:54.980 --> 00:11:59.400
Well, that's nice of you, but
don't expect any special treatment!

00:11:59.400 --> 00:12:01.240
Is there any news?

00:12:01.700 --> 00:12:06.030
The next time we mobilize,
it will end in hand-to-hand combat.

00:12:06.450 --> 00:12:10.200
I'll do my best, but I need
you to take care of my Ingram.

00:12:12.410 --> 00:12:13.790
Leave it to us.

00:12:20.340 --> 00:12:21.800
Have they made their move?

00:12:22.010 --> 00:12:23.260
Is it the Black Labor?

00:12:23.260 --> 00:12:24.090
Where?

00:12:24.470 --> 00:12:25.930
Not yet.

00:12:25.930 --> 00:12:28.050
Not yet?

00:12:28.560 --> 00:12:33.020
Every second is precious.
We may meet it in transit.

00:12:33.640 --> 00:12:36.480
Where should we set up?
Kisarazu or Kawasaki?

00:12:36.940 --> 00:12:38.440
What are you talking about?

00:12:39.270 --> 00:12:40.780
I'll explain on the way.

00:12:41.190 --> 00:12:46.200
Our destination is the
Babylon Project's Kawasaki Base...

00:12:46.200 --> 00:12:50.540
in order to intercept the
Black Labor. Prepare all vehicles!

00:12:50.830 --> 00:12:51.700
Roger.

00:12:57.500 --> 00:12:59.250
What a gloomy expression.

00:13:00.880 --> 00:13:02.090
It's just this pain in my ribs.

00:13:02.380 --> 00:13:04.470
Well, go home and get some rest.

00:13:05.470 --> 00:13:07.300
You won't let a wounded man
stand by his teammates?

00:13:07.970 --> 00:13:09.050
What was that?

00:13:09.470 --> 00:13:12.850
Oh, nothing. Nothing at all!

00:13:14.310 --> 00:13:19.940
I understand your feelings,
but these are special circumstances.

00:13:19.940 --> 00:13:22.820
Sometimes I have to face
disappointments too, you know.

00:13:27.740 --> 00:13:29.200
I request permission to come along.

00:13:29.490 --> 00:13:32.200
Get some rest.

00:13:32.200 --> 00:13:33.910
Captain!

00:13:38.790 --> 00:13:41.590
Don't look at me like that!

00:13:44.840 --> 00:13:47.010
All right! All right!

00:13:49.180 --> 00:13:49.970
Noa...

00:13:51.350 --> 00:13:54.560
When Noa's lost in concentration,
she only thinks of the present.

00:13:55.350 --> 00:13:57.310
- <i>You</i> have to plan her follow-through.
- Okay.

00:13:57.730 --> 00:14:00.690
And she's really pushing herself.

00:14:01.480 --> 00:14:03.150
Who's pushing?

00:14:03.690 --> 00:14:06.740
Noa. She's keeping a stiff
upper lip to distract herself.

00:14:07.070 --> 00:14:10.870
You think so? A stiff spine
can strengthen the whole soul.

00:14:11.410 --> 00:14:14.450
Maybe she's tougher than you think.

00:14:16.540 --> 00:14:17.790
What are you talking about?

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:23.710
I can't come with you.

00:14:24.670 --> 00:14:28.340
I'll just have to make up for you,
Kumagami, and Ota combined.

00:14:28.550 --> 00:14:29.300
I'm sorry.

00:14:29.720 --> 00:14:32.550
Dummy! Don't apologize for that!

00:14:38.350 --> 00:14:42.480
You're really going to use it?
I'm surprised they gave permission!

00:14:42.730 --> 00:14:44.770
It's easier to beg for forgiveness
than to ask for permission.

00:14:47.610 --> 00:14:52.030
She never likes to use these.

00:14:52.410 --> 00:14:57.330
I know, but we need everything
we've got against this foe.

00:14:58.660 --> 00:14:59.620
Hey, Shige!

00:15:01.040 --> 00:15:04.040
Open up locker 10 and load this up.

00:15:04.340 --> 00:15:09.510
Locker 10? You're kidding, aren't you?

00:15:21.100 --> 00:15:25.730
I want to send you out as
well armed as we can make you,

00:15:26.360 --> 00:15:29.900
and this is the biggest gun we have.

00:15:30.200 --> 00:15:32.320
But if I use it...

00:15:32.530 --> 00:15:35.870
I trust your judgment, Izumi.

00:15:37.450 --> 00:15:40.080
Why does my machine
have to be in the shop?

00:15:40.500 --> 00:15:44.920
Izumi, if you've got cold feet,
I'd be happy to take your place!

00:15:45.630 --> 00:15:47.250
It's all right, Ota.

00:15:49.050 --> 00:15:49.880
I can do it.

00:15:50.470 --> 00:15:51.680
We're fighting a monster.

00:15:52.130 --> 00:15:54.340
If you value your life,
you'll use every tool you've got.

00:16:12.360 --> 00:16:13.700
How's Bud holding up?

00:16:14.490 --> 00:16:17.530
He got plenty of sleep yesterday,
so he should be fine.

00:16:18.660 --> 00:16:19.660
Mr. Utsumi!

00:16:20.620 --> 00:16:22.620
I'll win this time, for sure!

00:16:23.080 --> 00:16:26.080
Of course you will.
We have no choice.

00:16:26.540 --> 00:16:28.340
You look like
you're enjoying this.

00:16:28.340 --> 00:16:31.010
Don't you feel any stress?

00:16:31.010 --> 00:16:33.550
Not a bit.

00:16:33.930 --> 00:16:36.640
So we're committed? Let's go.

00:16:51.860 --> 00:16:55.860
Retina identification complete.
Neural link: Active.

00:16:58.660 --> 00:17:00.160
Ready when you are!

00:17:09.290 --> 00:17:16.050
The <i>Sangria</i> is approaching.
Station the M5 Abrahams!

00:17:33.230 --> 00:17:36.700
Be extra careful of the construction.

00:17:37.360 --> 00:17:38.360
Don't worry.

00:17:40.450 --> 00:17:41.490
What did he say?

00:17:42.080 --> 00:17:43.620
He's a guard for the freighter coming in.

00:17:44.080 --> 00:17:46.920
And they brought
along four Labors? Why?

00:17:46.920 --> 00:17:50.590
Everyone's spooked after the
incident in Haruumi, yesterday.

00:17:53.670 --> 00:17:55.470
Their car is in the way.

00:17:55.800 --> 00:17:58.470
They're Babylon Project guards.

00:17:58.800 --> 00:18:00.850
They don't even have regular check-ins.

00:18:01.470 --> 00:18:04.060
Want me to move
them out of the way?

00:18:04.600 --> 00:18:06.560
Just draw them off.

00:18:08.940 --> 00:18:15.490
Listen up! That building is
about to catch fire. Handle it.

00:18:16.610 --> 00:18:20.950
What if he passes through
and enters Tokyo Bay?

00:18:22.780 --> 00:18:24.540
Losing your nerve?

00:18:25.660 --> 00:18:27.910
Just trying to second-guess Utsumi.

00:18:31.130 --> 00:18:32.380
Why aren't you guys eating?

00:18:33.130 --> 00:18:35.960
I don't have any appetite.

00:18:35.960 --> 00:18:38.340
Without an Ingram,
what can you do with that?

00:18:38.590 --> 00:18:43.810
Oh, this? A good police
officer can always improvise.

00:18:51.940 --> 00:18:55.570
Hello? This is Special
Vehicles, Second Section.

00:18:55.570 --> 00:18:57.820
Did something just happen
at the Babylon Project site?

00:18:59.450 --> 00:19:03.070
A fire?
There are no Labors fighting?

00:19:05.330 --> 00:19:06.290
I see.

00:19:08.120 --> 00:19:08.960
I think you heard everything.

00:19:09.460 --> 00:19:10.710
Was it an accident?

00:19:11.040 --> 00:19:13.670
It sounds like terrorists!

00:19:14.500 --> 00:19:16.380
It's probably Three-S.

00:19:18.760 --> 00:19:23.600
Kanuka, you're right. Utsumi will
make his stand at the Castle Gate.

00:19:42.570 --> 00:19:46.280
There they are!
They even brought out the M5's!

00:19:51.160 --> 00:19:53.250
There's Utsumi. Prepare to board!

00:19:53.710 --> 00:19:55.840
Sergeant! Look!

00:20:03.550 --> 00:20:05.090
He wouldn't!

00:20:05.850 --> 00:20:10.770
Impossible! Utsumi is exposing
the Griffin as he sails into port?

00:20:11.100 --> 00:20:12.940
He's crazy.

00:20:13.270 --> 00:20:16.730
You MUST NOT let him
through the Castle Gate!

00:20:17.320 --> 00:20:23.110
Understood, but at this point
we really can't settle it quietly.

00:20:23.110 --> 00:20:24.450
What?

00:20:27.990 --> 00:20:31.500
First Utsumi, now Three-S!
What are they thinking?

00:20:31.750 --> 00:20:32.960
This is...

00:20:33.210 --> 00:20:33.670
Huh?

00:20:34.460 --> 00:20:36.130
War.

00:21:13.450 --> 00:21:14.160
Look!

00:21:23.090 --> 00:21:26.470
The Black Labor!
Contact the station!

00:21:26.470 --> 00:21:27.050
Okay!

00:21:28.140 --> 00:21:31.760
Yes. Yes. I understand.

00:21:38.810 --> 00:21:40.940
They're landing on the Kisarazu side.

00:22:19.020 --> 00:22:19.900
All right.

00:22:20.480 --> 00:22:21.360
Here we go.

00:22:36.540 --> 00:22:39.580
Tonight, I'll fight to the bitter end.

00:22:43.960 --> 00:22:47.170
dakishimete MIDNIGHT BLUE
Just hold me tightly, Midnight Blue

00:22:47.300 --> 00:22:50.890
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:22:53.220 --> 00:22:57.140
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:23:04.570 --> 00:23:06.650
yume ni hikizurare
Pulled into my dream I find that I wake up

00:23:06.780 --> 00:23:09.570
ore wa ase mamire no Lonely
Drenched in sweat and feeling lonely

00:23:09.650 --> 00:23:14.160
hanashi-aite no TV suitchi hipparu
I turn off the TV I've been listening to

00:23:16.830 --> 00:23:18.830
ashita ichinichi wa
Tomorrow I will spend the whole day

00:23:18.910 --> 00:23:21.670
akogareta machi no gomi no naka
In the city of my dreams, amidst the old dust

00:23:21.920 --> 00:23:25.840
hayaku mein sutoriito ni sawaritai no sa
I want to feel the main street beneath my feet soon

00:23:29.010 --> 00:23:32.340
manazashi dake wa itsu demo
I plan to always look on the brighter side

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:37.600
ue wo muite 'ru tsumori
Keep my chin up, look to the future

00:23:37.560 --> 00:23:40.140
tatta hitotsu no michi da kara
After all, there's only one path I can travel

00:23:40.140 --> 00:23:43.350
dakishimete MIDNIGHT BLUE
